a first of its kind app is launching  here in las vegas to change how  fans enjoy live sports the creators of  love seats say the idea came from being  season tick  ticket holders for many teams over the  years  there was hundreds of empty seats every  single game and no way  to do anything about it besides people  sneaking forward which we won't do and  started to you know look at what can be  done about it and  you know with chatting with some of the  teams nothing really existed to be able  to solve our problem  this will launch next month for the  aviators opening game at las vegas  ballpark the app is a way for  fans to buy and sell tickets once  they're already at the event  all right so for example if it's let's  say the fifth inning and you want to  move closer to the field  you can look to see if maybe there's an  available seat  there's a flat fee on sales and pricing  changes in real time as that game  continues to go on  the big benefit is i mean if you don't  like your seats and you want to move you  want you want to  feel more like a vip or you want to be  behind the first base dugout or third  base dugout  it's really about all about maximizing  fan experience so giving the fans  everything they want being able to kind  of sit where they want  even though they maybe don't have the  best seats when the game starts they are  able to upgrade during the game  another use for the app is when you  leave a game early and want to make some  cash on an empty seat  or you want to move to sit with friends  love seeds is also in talks with the  golden knights and a few other  teams across the country
 

